Negative control for the reshaped `createTraceabilityCheck` (the NOT-YET verdict).

Grades a scenario NONE of whose own steps match as `partial` instead of `notYet`.
A capability written down and not yet driven is a legitimate state — under one
`.feature` per module it is the majority state — so this mutant turns every
un-stepped scenario into a failure and makes a shared implemented Background the
thing that reds the module.

The assertion that must go RED: the one asserting `partial` is empty over a
feature holding a scenario nothing matches (the module's own feature is one).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Proven RED 2026-08-12, blind
(`pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/scenario-harness exec vitest run src/steps/__tests__/traceability.test.ts`):
  x PASSES a scenario no step matches at all — a capability written down and not yet driven
      -> expected [] to strictly equal [ 'not driveable at all' ]
  x does not let a shared IMPLEMENTED Background make an un-stepped scenario partial
      -> expected [] to strictly equal [ 'written down, not yet driven' ]
  x FAILS a scenario matched only in part
      -> expected [ 'half driveable', 'not driveable at all' ] to strictly equal [ 'half driveable' ]
  3 failed | 10 passed. Reverted with `git apply -R`; suite back to 13 passed.

Behaviour shift measured by the author (NOT the red proof) — over
`client-email.feature`:
  before: driveable = 11, partial = 0,  notYet = 28
  after:  driveable = 11, partial = 28, notYet = 0

diff --git a/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts b/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
--- a/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
+++ b/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
@@ -335,7 +335,7 @@ export function createTraceabilityCheck(
     const ownMatched = drop(matched, scenario.backgroundStepCount);
 
     const verdict: Verdict = !some(ownMatched)
-      ? VERDICT.NOT_YET
+      ? VERDICT.PARTIAL
       : every(matched)
         ? VERDICT.DRIVEABLE
         : VERDICT.PARTIAL;
